                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5231/1044a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Original Spanish Draft Note Regarding the Labeling of
                        Sherry</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-sibling-dates" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1935-11-04T23:59:59+00:00" notBefore="1935-10-23T00:00:00+00:00"
                        >undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>Importations into the territories and possessions of the United States of America
                    of wines designated in any way by such words as “Jerez”, “Sherry”, “Xéres” shall
                    be accompanied by a certificate issued by the proper Spanish authorities
                    attesting that such wines are the product of Spain or the zone of growth and
                    production entitled to the use of such denominations and protected by the laws
                    and regulations of the Spanish Government.</p>
                <p>The said certificate will be required even when on the bottles or containers of
                    same the true origin of the product is mentioned or when the words “Jerez”,
                    “Sherry” or “Xéres” are accompanied by words such as “kind”, “type”, “manner”,
                    “rival”, “make” or any other specific regional indication or other.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
